tting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Manuel to remain Michigan AD until new hire is found","description":"Warde Manuel has agreed to stay in the job as Michigan's athletic director until the school finds a new athletic director, sources told ESPN on Wednesday.","published":"2026-11-25T16:12:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50592920/sources-manuel-stay-job-new-michigan-ad-hired","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4899488/amauri-washington","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A%27Mauri_Washington"},"pick":{"pick":33,"round":2,"team":"LAC","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"A'Mauri Washington","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A%27Mauri_Washington","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"A'Mauri Washington is an American college football defensive tackle for the Oregon Ducks.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Washington attended Oak Park High School in Oak Park, Michigan for his freshman and sophomore years before transferring to Chandler High School in Chandler, Arizona for his junior and senior years. He committed to the University of Oregon to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Washington was a backup his first two years at Oregon in 2023 and 2024, appearing in 22 games and recording 12 tackles. He became a starter for the first time his junior year in 2025."}]}}